extraction_notes: |
  Rifts World Book 3: England printed 46-50 (cache p047-p051, a text layer, page_offset 1). History 46-47, the Nog Henge and the notable dragons 47-48, the R.C.C. block 48-49, the Elixir 49-50. Read off renders of printed 48 (the R.C.C. head, attributes, M.D.C., psionics), 49 (bonuses, skills, tattoos, mystic study) and 152 (the ladder); every figure the cache gives agreed with the render.
  || ID: rifts-chiang-ku-dragon. chiang-ku-dragon is the Palladium Fantasy class (Dragons and Gods), untouched; this is a separate Rifts class, not a copy of it.
  || CREATURE: matches the chiang-ku-dragon-england creature row (row 9) on every racial figure: attributes, M.D.C. 4D4x100 (adult) and 1D4x100 (hatchling), P.P.E., I.S.P. 3D4x10, Horror Factor 13 and 9, and the bonuses. No difference found.
  || PLAYER STATUS: the entry states none (Note: stats for both the adult and the hatchling). Stored as a playable R.C.C., as the creature row is, with tags high-power.
  || XP: printed 152, read off a render, Chiang-Ku Dragon levels 1-15 stored as the lower bound of each band. The book continues as Ancient Chiang-ku, levels 16-26, which xp_table cannot hold: 16 800,001, 17 1,000,001, 18 1,250,001, 19 1,500,001, 20 2,000,001, 21 2,500,001, 22 3,000,001, 23 3,500,001, 24 4,000,001, 25 5,000,001, 26 6,000,001 (level 26 ends at 7,000,000). Level 15 ends at 800,000. The Palladium Fantasy class''s ladder (3,001, 5,001 ...) is a different book''s and is not this one.
  || VARIANTS: hatchling and adult, as the book prints both. The hatchling''s bonuses are only what the book gives it (+1 melee attack, +1 save vs all magic as spell_magic and ritual_magic, +2 vs Horror Factor); the adult''s are its own line. +4 damage is damage_bonus; the adult''s critical strike on 19-20 and +1 vs circle magic are a special ability and a saves.other row.
  || POOLS: M.D.C. is the human-form figure; the serpent form''s +1000 (adult) or +100 (hatchling) is a natural ability, not a second_form, which carries only S.D.C. and hit points. men_of_arms false, as for every race. I.S.P. 3D4x10 with no per-level gain printed.
  || PSIONICS: seven powers from ONE of the three categories is not a gate the block can state; categories_allowed names all three and the one-category rule is prose.
  || SKILLS: all domestic skills are the catalog''s Rifts core six (Cook, Dance, Fishing, Play Musical Instrument, Sewing, Sing) at catalog base; the Asian and Australian domestic rows of later books are left out (judgement call). Bonuses added to catalog bases. Two basic piloting skills: the book names no list; the civilian vehicles (judgement call). Three ancient and three modern W.P.: two named lists. The I.Q. bonus applying to all skills is the app''s ordinary rule.
  || HAND TO HAND: Basic, or two R.C.C. skills exchanged for Expert or Martial Arts; carried as hand_to_hand costs of 2. The class has no related skills of its own, so played alone the trade is not offered by the picker.
  || TATTOOS: catalog spells, tradition tattoo, named as the held rows are. Marks of Heritage: Eye of Knowledge (language) and Weapon Covered in Flames (the True Atlantean reading of the flaming sword). One tattoo from any category at levels 2-14 even: a spells_schedule from a list of every tattoo row not already granted. Tattoo master (Rose of Healing as Rose and Thorny Stem & Dripping Blood (heal), Phoenix Rising From the Flames (resurrection)): one option of a band-named Mystic Study pick carrying its bonuses (+1 vs all magic as spell_magic and ritual_magic, +1 vs Horror Factor, +2 P.E.) and those two tattoos; its two magic and two simple weapon tattoos and its per-level tattoos stay prose. No tattoo the entry names lacks a row.
  || MAGIC STUDY: the book''s percentages are the Mystic Study pick''s bands. Spells learned from a mage are not modelled: knows no spells unless taught, and what it learns is the teacher''s O.C.C. magic on this ladder; prose.
  || ELIXIR: the gear row chiang-ku-elixir-of-power-and-deceit (row 3), named in a special ability; not starting equipment, since the dragon brews it.
  || MONEY AND GEAR: 2D6x100 credits worth of gems or gold as starting_money; a set of clothing, an energy pistol and two ancient weapons as equipment, the last two from the catalog''s common sets.
