## Lore

The Chiang-Ku visited Earth some ten thousand years ago and adopted it as a favorite refuge between dimensional journeys. Fond of humankind, they lived among the people of Atlantis, Africa and China, first in human disguise and later openly, and taught dimensional travel and stone and tattoo magic to the Atlanteans, geomancy, astronomy and mathematics to the Chinese. When Atlantis vanished, hundreds of them died with it, and most of the survivors left as Earth''s magic waned. Those trapped behind lived out their lives in secret.

The dragons are near extinction, perhaps a hundred across the Megaverse. About two dozen have returned to Rifts Earth, and half of them live in England, where eleven pose as the tattooed druids called the Nog Henge, protectors of country folk and faerie folk. They recognize Mrrlyn as the old enemy foretold in prophecy and work quietly against him. Prrcyvel, a knight of New Camelot and friend to the young king, is one of them in disguise.

**Appearance:** an emerald green, six-legged lizard with a short tail, a slender angular head and a mouth of spike-like teeth, covered in triangular scales. All six feet have three toes with an opposable thumb and black claws, and the front legs serve as arms.

**Size (adult):** 12 to 20 feet (3.6 to 6.1 m) long, a quarter of it tail, about 4 feet (1.2 m) at the shoulder; 5 to 6 feet (1.5 to 1.8 m) tall in human form. Hatchlings are about 10% smaller.

**Weight (adult):** 200 lbs (90 kg) in human form, 1000 lbs (450 kg) in serpent form. Hatchlings are about 20% lighter.

**Average Life Span:** 6000 years.

## GM Notes

An adult is typically 1D6+7 levels of experience, always on this Dragon ladder whatever its magic. A Chiang-Ku is loyal and morally driven, and cannot keep out of trouble when people it has adopted are threatened; its usual method is subterfuge, setting kings and warriors into action from behind the scenes.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'rifts-chiang-ku-dragon');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'rifts-chiang-ku-dragon';

